  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 2ee87e681215b6147a44021cf30db039, type: 3}
  m_Name: "6.Jews\u2019 Sallyport"
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  nameOfPoint: "Jews\u2019 Sallyport"
  coordinatesPoint: {x: 14.515018, y: 35.90155}
  firstPartInfo: "The name of the caf\xE9\u2019 seems very familiar. I open Aline
    P\u2019Nina Tayar\u2019s book again to find where I had seen it. According to
    Tayar, in the 1600s, Malta was barred to Jewish believers. Only free Jews who
    acquired permission from the Grand Master of the Order could enter, and they
    would only be permitted to enter through the Jews\u2019 Sallyport. Still, Jewish
    people had to wear a yellow piece of cloth as identification. It was only in
    the 1800s under the British rule that free Jews were allowed to live permanently
    on the Maltese islands."
  secondPartInfo: "This seems to be only a glimpse into the history of the Maltese
    Jewish community. If I hadn\u2019t stumbled upon that photograph by chance, I
    wouldn\u2019t even have known that such a community existed in this country.\r\nAfter
    all these findings, the way Ondina Tayar is portrayed in that photograph is almost
    symbolic for the Jewish community in Malta: small and overshadowed. Still, like
    Ondina, they managed to hold their own through the hardship.\r"
  imgMarker: {fileID: 21300000, guid: c98feaebd40d8df449e6d3855ac84352, type: 3}
  imgMain: {fileID: 21300000, guid: f26fa8880b3aeef4b8516c82dc12f2a5, type: 3}
  nameOfStory: Jewish
  hintOfPOI: This is the final point of the story, you made it!
  solutionOfPOI: You are purrfect!
